findings.detail:
variant.h verbatim:
```
#undef LORA_SCK
#undef LORA_MISO
#undef LORA_MOSI
#undef LORA_CS

// https://www.waveshare.com/rp2040-lora.htm
// https://www.waveshare.com/img/devkit/RP2040-LoRa-HF/RP2040-LoRa-HF-details-11.jpg
#define LORA_SCK 14  // GPIO14
#define LORA_MISO 24 // GPIO24
#define LORA_MOSI 15 // GPIO15
#define LORA_CS 13   // GPIO13
```
platformio.ini build_flags include `-D HW_SPI1_DEVICE`. src/main.cpp (ARCH_RP2040 branch, ~line 970):
```
#ifdef HW_SPI1_DEVICE
    SPI1.setSCK(LORA_SCK);
    SPI1.setTX(LORA_MOSI);
    SPI1.setRX(LORA_MISO);
    pinMode(LORA_CS, OUTPUT);
    digitalWrite(LORA_CS, HIGH);
    SPI1.begin(false);
```
src/mesh/RadioInterface.cpp: `SPISettings loraSpiSettings(4000000, MSBFIRST, SPI_MODE0);` and `#elif defined(HW_SPI1_DEVICE) LockingArduinoHal *loraHal = new LockingArduinoHal(SPI1, loraSpiSettings);` → 4 MHz, MODE0, MSB-first. All four pins are legal RP2040 SPI1 pinmux functions (GP14=SPI1 SCK, GP15=SPI1 TX, GP24=SPI1 RX, GP13=SPI1 CSn), so this is a hardware-SPI-clean assignment on a custom RP2040 board.
